## Tips and common pitfalls

- **The most common mistake is arriving with three excellent sections.** Reviewers cannot tell you your scope is unbelievable if they cannot see your scope.
- **Mark your own weakest section before you hand it over.** A star next to the thinnest evidence tells your reviewer where to start and gets you a better review than a clean copy does.
- **Keep the marked-up copies.** You need scans or photos of both when you submit the final on {{ S09_DAY }}, {{ S09_DATE }}.

